  "goodToKnow": "Irritieren is a partial false friend. In German, it usually means to confuse or unsettle: Ich war irritiert means I was puzzled or taken aback, not necessarily annoyed. Lass dich nicht irritieren means don't let it put you off. It does mean to irritate physically: Das Mittel kann die Haut irritieren. For annoyance, Germans say ärgern or nerven. Die Irritation is confusion. Perfect without ge-: hat irritiert."
